let __v_222 = Value::from("Yes - soreness and stiffness for months after a joint replacement is normal, and it eases with the exercises rather than with rest: the joint is at its stiffest in the first six weeks and keeps loosening for up to a year, and a warm, puffy knee or hip after exercise is the usual reaction to doing more. Build up slowly, ice it for 15 minutes after the exercises, and keep the daily ones going even on a bad day. Ordinary swelling is around the joint; a calf or a whole leg that swells, goes hot or is tender to touch is not ordinary swelling - ring the ward or 111 the same day, because a clot is the thing to rule out. Ring about the joint too if it is hot and red, the wound leaks, or the pain gets worse each week rather than better.");
