let __v_231 = Value::from("Kneeling is the one thing many people never get back after a knee replacement: the new knee can take it, but the skin over it is numb and sore against a hard floor, so most people kneel on a cushion for a few minutes at a time rather than rule it out - try it on something soft once the wound is fully healed and the swelling has gone down. After a hip replacement you can kneel, but get down on the operated knee first and keep the new hip from bending past 90 degrees for the first few months. If kneeling is for gardening or a job, ask the physio to practise it with you rather than finding out on the day.");
