let __v_255 = Value::from("A shower is usually fine once the dressing is off and the wound is dry and sealed, and most wards send people home with a waterproof dressing so it can happen sooner - but a bath, a hot tub or a swim waits until the wound is fully closed, around two to six weeks, because standing water is where infection gets in. Pat the wound dry rather than rubbing it, leave it open to the air when you can, and put nothing on it - no creams, oils or powders. Ring the ward or 111 if the wound turns hot or red, leaks or smells, or the edges start to open.");
