let __v_292 = Value::from("A numb patch of skin around the scar is normal after a joint replacement and it often stays that way: the small nerves under the incision are cut on the way in, so the skin there feels wooden, tingly or dead to touch, and it usually softens over a year or two rather than meaning anything about the joint. An itchy scar is the same story - healing nerves - and so is a scar that pulls or feels tight. A scar that turns hot, red, weepy or spreads, or numbness that comes on suddenly or spreads up the leg, is the one to ring the ward or 111 about, the same day.");
